<title>CANADA: Scotiabank '96 loan loss unchanged from Q3.</title>
<headline>Scotiabank '96 loan loss unchanged from Q3.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Nova Scotia said on Wednesday that its 1996 provision for loan losses was C$380 million, unchanged from estimates in the previous third quarter.</p>
<p>The 1996 provision was down from C$560 million in 1995, the bank said in its year-end statement.</p>
<p>Scotiabank's general provision remained at C$325 million.</p>
<p>The bank said net impaired loans dropped 49 percent to C$743 million in 1996. Net impaired loans as a percentage of total loans and acceptances improved to 0.7 percent in 1996, their lowest level since 1989.</p>
<p>	  -- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
